msgvault keeps an offline, searchable archive of email, chat, and meeting
records. A daemon owns the archive: commands start or reuse a local daemon,
or use [remote].url from config.toml (--local forces the local daemon).

Start here:
  msgvault list-accounts --json    # id, email, type, counts, sync
  msgvault search 'from:alice@example.com newer_than:30d' --json
  # "id" feeds the commands below
  msgvault show-message <id> --json  # body_text, attachments
  msgvault export-eml <id> -o msg.eml  # export-attachments <id> -o DIR
  msgvault export-messages --start 2026-09-01T00:00:00Z --end 2026-10-01T00:00:00Z
  msgvault list-senders -n 20 --json  # also list-domains, list-labels
  msgvault stats
  msgvault person --help  # contacts
  msgvault daemon status
  msgvault setup status --json  # features and next steps

Output and exit status:
  --json prints JSON on stdout (export-messages prints JSON Lines). Progress and
  logs go to stderr; --log-level=warn quiets routine logs. Exit 0 success, 1 error,
  130 interrupted. 'msgvault quickstart' has a longer agent guide.

Usage:
  msgvault [command]

Search and read:
  list-accounts List archive accounts with type, message count, last sync
  list-domains  List top sender domains by message count
  list-labels   List all labels with message counts
  list-senders  List top senders by message count
  media         Search recording transcripts
  meetings      Read archived meeting context, actions, and metrics
  query         Run a SQL query against the analytics cache
  search        Search messages using Gmail-like query syntax
  show-message  Show full message details
  stats         Show archive message, thread, attachment and account totals
  tui           Open the interactive terminal UI

Export:
  create-subset      Create a smaller database from the archive
  export-attachment  Export an attachment by content hash
  export-attachments Export all attachments from a message as individual files
  export-discord     Export bounded Discord history from the local archive
  export-eml         Export a message as .eml file
  export-messages    Export messages in a time window as provider-neutral JSONL

People, organizations, and identity:
  attribute-definition Manage portable attribute definitions
  carddav              Manage CardDAV connections, books, and conflicts
  collection           Manage named groups of accounts
  employment           Manage employment records linking people and organizations
  identity             Manage the confirmed "me" identifiers for each account
  organization         Manage curated organizations and their employment records
  person               Find contacts and manage durable person profiles
  relationship-type    Manage person relationship types

Add and sync sources:
  add-account            Add a Gmail account via OAuth
  add-beeper             Add Beeper Desktop as an archive source
  add-calendar           Authorize Google Calendar and register its calendars
  add-carddav            Discover and configure a CardDAV account
  add-circleback         Authorize a Circleback account (browser OAuth)
  add-discord            Register Discord guilds for bot-based archival
  add-granola            Register a Granola account and validate its API key
  add-imap               Add an IMAP account
  add-matrix             Add a read-only Matrix account as an archive source
  add-muesli             Register a local Muesli meeting database
  add-notion-meetings    Register and validate a Notion AI Meeting Notes source
  add-o365               Add a Microsoft 365 account via OAuth
  add-plaud              Authorize and register a Plaud cloud account
  add-slack              Add a Slack workspace as an archive source
  add-synctech-sms-drive Configure a Google Drive SMS Backup & Restore source
  add-teams              Authorize Microsoft Teams (delegated Graph) for an account
  add-twenty             Register and validate a Twenty Call Recorder source
  add-twilio             Register and validate a Twilio call source
  archive-remote-images  Download remote images in archived email (needs consent)
  backfill-beeper-media  Retry pending Beeper attachment downloads
  backfill-discord-media Retry pending Discord attachment downloads
  backfill-slack-media   Retry pending Slack file downloads
  backfill-teams-media   Re-fetch missing Teams inline images for imported messages
  list-folders           List IMAP folders (mailboxes) available for an account
  muesli-hook            Sync the meeting named by a Muesli completion event
  remove-account         Remove an account and all its data
  sync                   Sync new mail from Gmail, IMAP, and Microsoft accounts
  sync-beeper            Sync chats from Beeper Desktop (all connected networks)
  sync-calendar          Sync Google Calendar events for an account
  sync-carddav           Synchronize enabled CardDAV connections
  sync-circleback        Sync Circleback meetings, notes, and transcripts
  sync-discord           Sync registered Discord guild history
  sync-full              Perform a full sync of Gmail accounts
  sync-granola           Sync Granola meeting notes and transcripts
  sync-matrix            Sync joined rooms from Matrix
  sync-muesli            Sync meetings from a local Muesli database
  sync-notion-meetings   Sync Notion AI Meeting Notes
  sync-plaud             Sync Plaud recordings, transcripts, and notes
  sync-slack             Sync Slack conversations (channels, group DMs, DMs)
  sync-synctech-sms      Run one configured synctech-sms source now
  sync-teams             Sync Microsoft Teams chats and channels
  sync-twenty            Sync Twenty Call Recorder meetings
  sync-twilio            Sync Twilio calls and recordings
  update-account         Update account settings
  verify                 Verify archive integrity against Gmail

Import local exports:
  import-eml          Import a tree of RFC 5322 .eml files
  import-emlx         Import Apple Mail .emlx files into msgvault
  import-gvoice       Import Google Voice history from Takeout export
  import-imazing-csv  Import Messages CSV exports created by iMazing
  import-imessage     Import iMessages from local database
  import-maildir      Import a Maildir or Maildir++ archive
  import-mbox         Import an MBOX export into msgvault
  import-messenger    Import Facebook Messenger from a Meta data export
  import-pst          Import a PST (Outlook) archive into msgvault
  import-slackdump    Import a Slackdump export
  import-synctech-sms Import SMS Backup & Restore exports
  import-whatsapp     Import WhatsApp messages from an Android or Apple database

Drafts, calendar, and Kata (write to providers):
  calendar      Control live calendar events and query availability
  draft-compose Create an email, native Beeper, or local chat draft
  draft-delete  Delete a managed draft
  draft-edit    Replace the body of a managed draft
  draft-forward Create an IMAP draft forwarding an archived message
  draft-get     Read a managed draft or list a chat's local drafts
  draft-recover Recover an interrupted managed IMAP draft edit or delete
  draft-reply   Create an IMAP or Gmail reply draft from an archived message
  draft-send-as List Gmail send-as identities
  kata          Create Kata issues that quote archived evidence

Review and delete:
  cancel-deletion Cancel pending or in-progress deletion batches
  deduplicate     Find and merge duplicate messages within an account
  delete-deduped  Permanently delete dedup-hidden messages locally
  delete-staged   Execute staged deletions
  gc              Purge source-deleted messages and compact the SQLite archive
  list-deletions  List pending and recent deletion batches
  show-deletion   Show details of a deletion batch
  stage-delete    Stage messages matching a query or IDs for deletion

Indexes, embeddings, and analytics cache:
  activity    Build the derived activity spine
  build-cache Build analytics cache for fast TUI queries
  cache-stats Show statistics about the analytics cache
  documents   Manage document attachment indexing
  embeddings  Manage message vector embeddings
  eval        Score search quality against relevance judgments (qrels)
  multimodal  Manage and search visual attachment embeddings
  rebuild-fts Rebuild the full-text search index from scratch

Maintenance and repair:
  backup               Back up the archive to a snapshot repository
  init-db              Initialize the database schema
  pack-attachments     Pack loose attachment files into sealed pack files
  purge-excluded-media Reclaim locally stored media excluded by current policy
  repack-attachments   Reclaim dead bytes from sparse attachment packs
  repair-dates         Repair missing or implausible email sent dates
  repair-derived       Re-derive message text and metadata from stored payloads
  repair-encoding      Repair invalid UTF-8 encoding in message text fields
  repair-identity      Confirm account identities and recompute is_from_me
  repair-labels        Rebuild IMAP message labels from stored mailbox memberships
  repair-list-ids      Repair archived email List-Id values from raw MIME
  repair-message       Repair one Gmail message snapshot or audit stored Gmail MIME
  repair-senders       Restore missing email senders from archived MIME
  unpack-attachments   Restore packed attachments to loose files

Setup, daemon, and integrations:
  agent-token  Manage restricted agent grant tokens
  completion   Generate shell completion script
  credentials  Manage provider credentials on the daemon host
  daemon       Manage the background daemon
  export-token Export OAuth token to a remote msgvault instance
  help         Help about any command
  logs         View and tail msgvault's structured log files
  mcp          Run MCP server for Claude Desktop integration
  openapi      Print the msgvault OpenAPI schema
  quickstart   Print a quickstart guide for AI agents
  serve        Run msgvault as a daemon with scheduled sync
  setup        Run first-time setup; 'setup status' shows enabled features
  skills       Manage agent skills for coding assistants
  update       Update msgvault to the latest version
  version      Print version information

Flags:
      --agent-allow-insecure      Allow plain HTTP for agent-delegated connections (trusted networks only)
      --agent-token-file string   Path to a file containing the agent grant secret (requires --agent-url)
      --agent-url string          Daemon URL for agent-delegated mode (requires --agent-token-file)
      --config string             config file (default: ~/.msgvault/config.toml)
  -h, --help                      help for msgvault
      --home string               home directory (overrides MSGVAULT_HOME)
      --local                     use local daemon instead of configured remote
      --log-file string           override log file path (default: <data dir>/logs/msgvault-YYYY-MM-DD.log)
      --log-level string          log level: debug, info, warn, error (default: info)
      --log-sql                   log every SQL query at info level (verbose; for debugging)
      --log-sql-slow-ms int       threshold in ms above which a SQL query is logged as slow (default 100; 0 uses the default)
      --no-log-file               disable the log file for this run (stderr output stays on)
  -v, --verbose                   verbose output (implies --log-level=debug)

Use "msgvault [command] --help" for more information about a command.
